-- title:
--   Lifting N-element local generation of J from the special fibre
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative local noetherian ring with residue field $\kappa =$ `IsLocalRing.ResidueField R`, let $N$ be a natural number and let $J$ be an ideal of the polynomial ring $R[x_i : i \in \mathrm{Fin}\,N]$ such that the quotient $R[x]/J$ is a finite and flat $R$-module. Write $\bar J$ for the image of $J$ under the coefficientwise reduction map $R[x] \to \kappa[x]$ induced by `IsLocalRing.residue R`, i.e. `Ideal.map (MvPolynomial.map (IsLocalRing.residue R)) J`. Assume the fibrewise hypothesis: for every maximal ideal $\bar{\mathfrak n}$ of $\kappa[x]$ containing $\bar J$, there exist $g_i \in \bar J$ ($i \in \mathrm{Fin}\,N$) whose images in the localisation $\kappa[x]_{\bar{\mathfrak n}}$ generate the ideal generated there by $\bar J$. The conclusion is that for every maximal ideal $\mathfrak n$ of $R[x]$ containing $J$ there exist $g_i \in J$ ($i \in \mathrm{Fin}\,N$) such that the ideal generated by $J$ in the localisation $R[x]_{\mathfrak n}$ equals the span of the images of the $g_i$; so local generation by exactly $N$ elements, indexed by the same finite set as the variables, lifts from the special fibre to $R[x]$.
--
--   This is a Nakayama-type descent of local generation along the flat finite quotient $R[x]/J$: generators of the ideal of the special fibre lift to generators after localisation at a maximal ideal of $R[x]$. It is used in constructing presentations of the levels of a $p$-divisible group over a ring of integers, by [`PDivisibleGroup.exists_square_presentation_level_of_ringOfIntegers`](thm.html#PDivisibleGroup.exists_square_presentation_level_of_ringOfIntegers).
-- source:
